# AGENTS.md

{{name}}: a Vue single page app (SPA). `npm run build` turns it into static files (`index.html` plus JS and CSS in
`dist/`) that a separate backend serves. There is no server code in this repository, the backend API is reached under
`/api`.

Stack: Vite, Vue 3 (`<script setup lang="ts">`), TypeScript, Vue Router, TanStack Query (server data), Pinia (client
state), Tailwind CSS v4, Vitest with Vue Test Utils, Biome.

## Commands

```bash
npm install
npm run dev          # dev server on http://localhost:5173 with hot reload
npm run build        # type check (vue-tsc) and production build into dist/
npm test             # all unit and component tests once
npm run test:watch   # tests in watch mode
npm run typecheck    # vue-tsc only
npm run check        # biome format + lint with fixes, then vue-tsc
```

Before you finish a change, `npm run check` and `npm test` must pass.

## Where things are

```
src/
  main.ts               entry point, installs Pinia, the router and TanStack Query
  App.vue               the layout around the current page
  router/index.ts       the list of routes, the only place that maps URLs to pages
  pages/                one component per page, referenced by router/index.ts
  features/<feature>/   one vertical slice per topic, see below
  components/ui/        shared, generic building blocks (BaseButton, BaseCard), no feature logic
  components/layout/    the app frame: header, navigation, footer
  lib/                  shared infrastructure: api-client.ts (fetch wrapper), query-client.ts
  stores/               global client state used by many features (theme)
  assets/images|fonts/  images and fonts imported by code or CSS
  styles/app.css        Tailwind entry, design tokens in @theme
  test/                 test setup
  config.ts             constants that are the same in every environment
public/                 files served as they are under a fixed URL (favicon, robots.txt)
```

## Features (vertical slices)

Everything that belongs to one topic lives in `src/features/<feature>/`, so a feature can be understood, changed and
deleted in one place:

```
features/<feature>/
  api/          queryOptions, useQuery/useMutation composables and the request functions (via lib/api-client)
  components/   components of this feature, with their *.spec.ts next to them
  stores/       Pinia stores only this feature uses
  types.ts      types of this feature (optional)
```

- Only create the subfolders a feature needs.
- A feature may import from `components/`, `lib/`, `stores/` and `config.ts`, but not from another feature. If two
  features need the same code, move it to `components/` or `lib/`.
- Pages stay thin: a page in `src/pages` receives route params as props and renders feature components.

## How to add things

- **Page:** add a component in `src/pages` (e.g. `src/pages/orders/OrderPage.vue`) and a route in
  `src/router/index.ts`, lazy loaded with `component: () => import(...)`. Use `props: true` to get params as props.
- **API call:** add `features/<feature>/api/<name>.ts` with `queryOptions` and a composable, using `api.get/post/...`
  from `@/lib/api-client`. Paths are relative to `/api`. See `features/health/api/health.ts`.
- **Server data** always goes through TanStack Query, never into a Pinia store.
- **Client state** (UI state, drafts): a Pinia setup store in the feature, or in `src/stores` if it is global.
- **Shared component:** `src/components/ui`, styled with Tailwind classes, no data fetching.
- **Styling:** Tailwind utility classes in the template; new colors or fonts as tokens in `@theme` in `styles/app.css`.

## Conventions

- Imports use the `@/` alias for `src/`.
- Components are single file components named in PascalCase (`HealthStatus.vue`), other files in camelCase or
  kebab-case.
- Tests are `*.spec.ts` next to the code. Mount with `mount()` from `@vue/test-utils` and pass the needed plugins
  (Pinia, router, `VueQueryPlugin`) via `global.plugins`, see `router/router.spec.ts`. Stub `fetch` instead of calling a
  backend.
- Environment settings are in `.env.example` (copy to `.env.local`). Only `VITE_*` variables reach the browser.
- TypeScript stays on version 6 until `vue-tsc` supports TypeScript 7.
